1
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:56,799
Who is he?

2
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,959
Chinese. A mercenary.

3
00:01:59,879 --> 00:02:01,200
A top-tier sniper.

4
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:05,239
He's seen combat in many countries.

5
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:08,000
He's extremely experienced.

6
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,960
He's the eyes of the Silent Protectors.

7
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:12,919
Before we strike, we must systematically clip

8
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,560
Wei Tian's wings.

9
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,560
Is he really that good?

10
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:17,039
I doubt it.

11
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:18,840
Don't underestimate what he's capable of.

12
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:22,080
He's thwarted our operations multiple times.

13
00:02:22,759 --> 00:02:23,879
The reason I brought you in

14
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,240
is that you're both top-tier snipers.

15
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,000
I don't intend to lose to anyone.

16
00:02:30,479 --> 00:02:33,719
This one, a hot-tempered girl,

17
00:02:35,439 --> 00:02:36,879
and this Chinese guy,

18
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:41,080
an employee at the Plato Hotel—

19
00:02:41,759 --> 00:02:44,520
we must eliminate them all, one by one.

20
00:02:56,319 --> 00:02:57,120
Mr. Xiao.

21
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:59,479
This isn't a theft or a missing persons case.

22
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,960
It's just a hotel management issue.

23
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,039
You can't pin the blame on Zhong An.

24
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:04,719
Xiang Bei,

25
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,599
Such an expensive bottle of wine went missing.

26
00:03:07,879 --> 00:03:10,080
How could that be a management issue?

27
00:03:10,879 --> 00:03:12,080
Such an expensive bottle of wine...

28
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,919
Isn't that hotel property?

29
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:15,199
Our property was lost,

30
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:16,960
so of course it's a security issue!

31
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,960
Protecting our hotel staff

32
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,879
and protecting our property from loss...

33
00:03:20,879 --> 00:03:22,840
that's all in our security agreement.

34
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,560
Right?

35
00:03:26,159 --> 00:03:29,520
So finding this bottle is your responsibility.

36
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,319
Captain.

37
00:03:39,639 --> 00:03:42,120
I found this bullet in my car.

38
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,159
Let's go.

39
00:03:52,319 --> 00:03:55,039
This is already the third time.

40
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,319
And the fiercest one yet.

41
00:03:58,639 --> 00:04:00,639
Yet he didn't hit us with a single shot.

42
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,759
This bullet was specially modified.

43
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,599
Anyone who can make a bullet like this

44
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,759
must be a top-tier sniper.

45
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,160
And he wouldn't miss.

46
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,800
It seems this hitman

47
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:20,399
didn't really want to kill you.

48
00:04:21,439 --> 00:04:22,720
At least, he hesitated.

49
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,399
So, what did you want to see me for?

50
00:04:28,879 --> 00:04:30,079
Even buying me a drink...

51
00:04:30,319 --> 00:04:31,680
You definitely need a favor.

52
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:32,959
I... No, I don't.

53
00:04:32,959 --> 00:04:37,600
I genuinely just wanted to treat you to a drink.

54
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,160
Shifty eyes, stammering speech...

55
00:04:43,839 --> 00:04:45,360
You're clearly lying.

56
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:50,240
Well, there's been some trouble at the hotel lately.

57
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,160
A female client

58
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:55,720
stored a bottle of wine with us a year ago.

59
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,759
Now it's missing,

60
00:04:56,759 --> 00:04:58,160
and she wants to file a complaint.

61
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,360
Legally speaking,

62
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:04,399
the key issue here

63
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:06,680
is whether it's management negligence

64
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,040
or an inside job.

65
00:05:08,959 --> 00:05:10,839
Or maybe both.

66
00:05:12,439 --> 00:05:14,120
If she takes you to court...

67
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:15,319
No way.

68
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,600
That bottle was signed by her fiancé.

69
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,160
I don't even know where to begin looking.

70
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,319
I mean... I was thinking,

71
00:05:22,319 --> 00:05:26,959
you're so smart, can you help me out?

72
00:05:30,839 --> 00:05:32,079
In our line of work,

73
00:05:32,279 --> 00:05:33,560
the first step is always to gather

74
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,759
sufficient information and materials.

75
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:42,519
I have some of his paintings here,

76
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,879
and some newspapers from his place.

77
00:05:47,959 --> 00:05:49,160
And here is

78
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:51,800
the wine storage registry.

79
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,839
Right here.

80
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:09,360
He's a painter.

81
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:11,160
Her fiancé is a painter too.

82
00:06:17,199 --> 00:06:20,480
First, you have to imagine you're

83
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,040
Luo Qingxuan's fiancé.

84
00:06:22,759 --> 00:06:23,560
And then,

85
00:06:25,199 --> 00:06:26,720
follow every path he took in life,

86
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,839
and walk it all over again.

87
00:06:29,319 --> 00:06:30,800
Walk it all over again?

88
00:06:32,439 --> 00:06:34,399
Yes, walk it all over again.

89
00:06:35,079 --> 00:06:37,199
If you were her fiancé,

90
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,399
where would you go?

91
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:35,199
What are you looking at, Uncle Qu?

92
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:39,120
Seeing if it brings back any memories.

93
00:07:41,959 --> 00:07:43,720
Does this painting look familiar?

94
00:07:45,839 --> 00:07:47,439
Want to buy it?

95
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,839
But...

96
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,680
it looks pretty expensive.

97
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,040
If you want to find something out,

98
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,800
you've got to invest something first.

99
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,839
Maybe he'll reimburse you.

100
00:07:59,439 --> 00:08:01,120
Would Mr. Xiao really reimburse this?

101
00:08:40,519 --> 00:08:41,480
Found it.

102
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,039
I'll send a photo to Wei Tian.

103
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:43,799
Take it, quick.

104
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:48,919
Send it to him.

105
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:51,919
Okay.

106
00:08:51,919 --> 00:08:52,679
Okay, let's go.

107
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,399
I found the item.

108
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,799
What's this?

109
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:02,799
I can guarantee

110
00:10:02,879 --> 00:10:04,200
that with this,

111
00:10:04,399 --> 00:10:05,200
that guest

112
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,039
won't dare give the hotel trouble anymore.

113
00:10:09,399 --> 00:10:11,759
What kind of trick are you pulling?

114
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:12,840
So,

115
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,360
wanna come with me

116
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,480
to witness this decisive moment?

117
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:19,279
There's quite a story behind this.

118
00:10:19,480 --> 00:10:20,440
Of course I do.

119
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:21,320
A secret.

120
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,600
Alright, let's return this secret to its owner.

121
00:10:26,519 --> 00:10:28,440
Okay, I'm heading out.

122
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,600
Rosie, be careful.

123
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,200
A while back,

124
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,759
a sniper took shots at Rosie.

125
00:10:41,559 --> 00:10:43,600
He missed every time.

126
00:10:45,399 --> 00:10:47,879
The guy wears black

127
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,960
and carries a cello case.

128
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:52,799
He's tall,

129
00:10:52,799 --> 00:10:53,879
about my height.

130
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,879
Can you use your Zhong An network

131
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,879
to track this guy down for me?

132
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,960
Sure, got it.

133
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:09,320
You actually found this painting.

134
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,480
This is the scene of our first meeting.

135
00:11:17,879 --> 00:11:18,840
Over here,

136
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:20,679
we also found a gift

137
00:11:21,159 --> 00:11:22,639
left by your fiancé.

138
00:11:24,039 --> 00:11:24,879
Right here.

139
00:11:29,759 --> 00:11:30,600
That painting

140
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:33,559
was painted by the man for his beloved.

141
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,519
He sent it to be framed,

142
00:11:34,759 --> 00:11:36,960
but tragically got into a car crash.

143
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,840
The painting remained stored away.

144
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,559
Over time,

145
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:43,440
somehow

146
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,759
it ended up at the auction.

147
00:11:47,159 --> 00:11:49,279
If not for this wine incident,

148
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:51,600
the painting might have hung there much longer.

149
00:11:51,679 --> 00:11:53,480
She'd never have known his feelings.

150
00:11:54,279 --> 00:11:55,200
She would've known.

151
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,240
As long as one has a good heart,

152
00:11:58,639 --> 00:12:00,799
heaven will make things right.

153
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,399
Wei Tian,

154
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,080
if anything happens in the future,

155
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,799
you must tell me.

156
00:12:14,799 --> 00:12:15,799
Don't keep secrets from me.

157
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,360
Tell me even the smallest things.

158
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:21,919
Even if a cockroach shows up?

159
00:12:23,879 --> 00:12:24,679
For that...

160
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,759
just stomp it dead.

161
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:05,879
Maurice.

162
00:13:11,039 --> 00:13:11,840
Move.

163
00:13:15,279 --> 00:13:17,480
How are you? Are you alright?

164
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,200
I'm fine.

165
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,720
Be more careful.

166
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,720
Why did you interfere with my mission?

167
00:13:29,879 --> 00:13:31,360
I'll handle my own target.

168
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,639
Your room

169
00:13:32,639 --> 00:13:34,600
is covered with maps of that woman's routes,

170
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:37,240
yet you still haven't made a move.

171
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,039
Why?

172
00:13:38,039 --> 00:13:39,759
I said I'll kill her.

173
00:13:39,759 --> 00:13:41,200
I'll complete my mission.

174
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,519
Casablanca Bar

175
00:13:43,519 --> 00:13:45,480
is where that woman often goes.

176
00:13:45,559 --> 00:13:47,279
You should know better than I do

177
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:49,600
where the best sniper spot is.

178
00:13:51,159 --> 00:13:52,039
I know.

179
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:53,840
This is your last chance.

180
00:13:54,279 --> 00:13:55,519
If the mission fails,

181
00:13:55,759 --> 00:13:57,320
Hades will kill you.

182
00:13:57,559 --> 00:14:00,080
I'm sure you know the syndicate's rules.

183
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,279
Charon has developed feelings for the target.

184
00:14:12,559 --> 00:14:13,360
I think

185
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:15,679
he can no longer carry out this mission.

186
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:18,320
Alright, I know.

187
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:59,519
What can I get you to drink, sir?

188
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,159
Coffee.

189
00:15:06,559 --> 00:15:07,240
I'm sorry.

190
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,080
We don't serve coffee here, only alcohol.

191
00:15:10,559 --> 00:15:12,080
Don't you have a coffee pot right there?

192
00:15:12,519 --> 00:15:13,320
That thing...

193
00:15:13,519 --> 00:15:15,000
I... I really don't know how to use it.

194
00:15:15,159 --> 00:15:15,879
If you want coffee,

195
00:15:15,879 --> 00:15:17,879
I can make you some instant coffee.

196
00:15:19,879 --> 00:15:20,679
I know how.

197
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:22,440
I'll do it myself.

198
00:15:24,519 --> 00:15:26,440
It's just a coffee. No need for that much.

199
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:34,399
Alright, help yourself then.

200
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:36,799
Thanks.

201
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,000
This is the second time I've seen

202
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,160
someone drink coffee this way.

203
00:17:56,519 --> 00:17:57,359
The second time?

204
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:58,519
Yeah.

205
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:38,359
I remember now, Rosie. It was you.

206
00:18:46,359 --> 00:18:48,039
Sir, what's wrong?

207
00:18:56,279 --> 00:18:58,000
Sir, wh-what's wrong?

208
00:18:59,119 --> 00:19:00,160
Are you okay, sir?

209
00:19:00,839 --> 00:19:01,640
Are you all right?

210
00:19:01,839 --> 00:19:02,640
No...

211
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:07,279
Sir, your money!

212
00:19:07,559 --> 00:19:08,359
Money...

213
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,599
Maurice, get out here!

214
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:29,880
Charon, you're digging your own grave.

215
00:20:30,839 --> 00:20:32,480
Hades won't let you get away with this.

216
00:20:51,359 --> 00:20:53,759
Charon, even if you kill me,

217
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:56,039
he'll send more people to hunt you down.

218
00:20:56,039 --> 00:20:57,400
You won't get away either.

219
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:19,440
That year,

220
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,640
this is where we first met.

221
00:21:22,599 --> 00:21:24,000
He came here to sketch,

222
00:21:24,759 --> 00:21:26,119
while I was picking grapes.

223
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:30,160
I was instantly captivated by his focused look.

224
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,799
Love at first sight.

225
00:21:33,839 --> 00:21:37,519
Love often starts as a cliché,

226
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:41,240
yet it's always so moving.

227
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:45,839
Time is fleeting,

228
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:50,559
but the scenes in my memory never fade.

229
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,440
This is the barrel of wine.

230
00:22:11,559 --> 00:22:13,400
Did he really leave this for me?

231
00:22:14,039 --> 00:22:16,039
It has the date written on it,

232
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,000
and his signature.

233
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,559
You wouldn't have forgotten.

234
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:23,640
I've finally found you again.

235
00:22:24,839 --> 00:22:26,160
Good thing you're here.

236
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:29,400
You've always been here.

237
00:22:32,279 --> 00:22:34,640
I think he left this barrel of wine...

238
00:22:35,359 --> 00:22:37,359
...to surprise you and bring you joy.

239
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:39,359
He wouldn't want to see you sad.

240
00:22:40,279 --> 00:22:41,079
Alright.

241
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,119
Then let's throw a party

242
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,480
and drink this barrel.

243
00:23:12,359 --> 00:23:13,160
Xiao Bei.

244
00:23:13,519 --> 00:23:14,920
This is the Hades Syndicate's

245
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,319
most active hitman.

246
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:17,640
Asian features.

247
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:19,839
Around 1.85 meters tall.

248
00:23:20,559 --> 00:23:21,519
When he strikes,

249
00:23:21,799 --> 00:23:23,039
he likes to use a cello case

250
00:23:23,039 --> 00:23:24,480
to conceal his sniper rifle.

251
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,880
His hits have spanned several countries.

252
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:28,759
He's extremely dangerous.

253
00:23:28,759 --> 00:23:29,720
Okay, I understand.

254
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:39,759
Very good.

255
00:23:40,759 --> 00:23:41,759
I'm very pleased.

256
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,680
In this wine,

257
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:58,599
you can taste longing.

258
00:23:59,960 --> 00:24:02,759
All those years are captured in it.

259
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:08,079
Sometimes, I feel like

260
00:24:09,480 --> 00:24:11,240
this is a very familiar scene,

261
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,960
yet I can't remember anything at all.

262
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:16,240
After all these years,

263
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:17,960
even though some memories have returned,

264
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:20,200
there is still a crucial part

265
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,240
that hasn't come back.

266
00:24:22,319 --> 00:24:23,119
Tell me,

267
00:24:24,079 --> 00:24:25,359
if I leave this place,

268
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,160
might I actually remember more?

269
00:24:31,160 --> 00:24:34,200
Rosie, I think

270
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:38,279
what you need is to be happy,

271
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:40,200
to help you recover your lost memories.

272
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:41,079
So,

273
00:24:42,279 --> 00:24:43,279
as long as you're happy,

274
00:24:44,279 --> 00:24:45,119
going anywhere,

275
00:24:46,079 --> 00:24:47,480
or leaving the Silent Protectors at any time,

276
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:50,039
is completely fine.

277
00:24:51,079 --> 00:24:53,160
In the end, everyone has their own choices.

278
00:24:54,119 --> 00:24:54,920
Really.

279
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:06,359
You two talk. I'll go check over there.

280
00:25:12,559 --> 00:25:13,920
Is Rosie all right?

281
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:14,920
She's fine. Have a seat.

282
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:21,119
She said having some red wine

283
00:25:22,039 --> 00:25:25,000
seemed to spark some of her memories.

284
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:26,759
So you see,

285
00:25:27,039 --> 00:25:29,599
a little red wine now and then is a good thing.

286
00:25:36,759 --> 00:25:37,559
What's up?

287
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:39,680
Wei Tian,

288
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:43,480
I actually got

289
00:25:43,599 --> 00:25:45,680
a wine tasting certificate.

290
00:25:48,279 --> 00:25:49,079
So,

291
00:25:49,599 --> 00:25:52,079
I plan to stay in Antilocaris

292
00:25:52,359 --> 00:25:53,400
for the long haul.

293
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:56,680
But I hope

294
00:25:57,519 --> 00:25:58,799
I can also become

295
00:26:00,160 --> 00:26:01,759
a part of the Silent Protectors.

296
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:04,480
The Silent Protectors family

297
00:26:05,599 --> 00:26:08,119
already considers you one of us.

298
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:10,880
As long as you stay safe,

299
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:12,680
that's what matters most.

300
00:26:14,519 --> 00:26:16,559
Was the test hard?

301
00:26:18,359 --> 00:26:19,319
It... it was okay.

302
00:26:19,599 --> 00:26:20,400
Not bad.

303
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,200
This wine is really good.

304
00:26:24,279 --> 00:26:25,079
Thank you.

305
00:26:25,079 --> 00:26:25,640
You're welcome.

306
00:26:25,640 --> 00:26:27,279
I really must thank you this time

307
00:26:27,279 --> 00:26:28,400
for retrieving this barrel of wine for me.

308
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:29,079
Don't mention it.

309
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:30,240
I'm truly grateful.

310
00:27:36,839 --> 00:27:38,319
Hello, can I try it?

311
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:37,039
Thank you.

312
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:51,680
I heard this wine was aged in oak barrels

313
00:28:51,799 --> 00:28:52,799
for three years.

314
00:28:55,079 --> 00:28:55,880
Good wine.

315
00:28:57,119 --> 00:28:58,279
Do you know a lot about wine?

316
00:28:58,880 --> 00:28:59,720
Not really.

317
00:28:59,839 --> 00:29:01,640
Wine doesn't need understanding, just love.

318
00:29:02,559 --> 00:29:03,400
To good wine.

319
00:29:04,039 --> 00:29:04,839
To love.

320
00:29:13,119 --> 00:29:13,920
You know what?

321
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:16,599
There was a man who, for the woman he loved,

322
00:29:17,039 --> 00:29:18,359
made wine for three years.

323
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:20,000
Yet in the end...

324
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,960
the wine remained, but the person was gone.

325
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:27,200
You can taste the longing. All that time is in the wine.

326
00:29:40,119 --> 00:29:41,440
Sorry, if you'll excuse me.

327
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,559
May I borrow your instrument for a moment?

328
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:22,400
If you don't mind me asking,

329
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:26,039
does this necklace you're wearing

330
00:32:27,039 --> 00:32:30,000
hold any special meaning?

331
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:21,680
No.

332
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:25,880
I bought this yesterday at a small shop.

333
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:32,279
I have one almost just like it.

334
00:33:33,759 --> 00:33:34,559
What a coincidence.

335
00:33:44,559 --> 00:33:47,720
Have we met somewhere before?

336
00:33:51,839 --> 00:33:52,640
I'm sorry.

337
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:54,400
I was injured before,

338
00:33:55,079 --> 00:33:57,039
and there's a lot I can't remember.

339
00:33:57,880 --> 00:34:00,400
If you know who I am, could you tell me?

340
00:34:02,519 --> 00:34:03,319
I don't know you.

341
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:05,240
But...

342
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:07,799
that piece we just played together...

343
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,440
That piece is very famous.

344
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:11,719
A lot of people know how to play it.

345
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,480
Yet I've only ever heard one person

346
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,920
play it on the cello.

347
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:17,320
Plenty of people play the cello too.

348
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,320
Where are you from?

349
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:21,480
I'm Chinese.

350
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:22,360
More specifically?

351
00:34:23,519 --> 00:34:24,599
I can't remember.

352
00:34:25,599 --> 00:34:26,400
Who are you?

353
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:58,559
The hostess of today's party

354
00:34:59,519 --> 00:35:00,760
and her fiancé

355
00:35:01,559 --> 00:35:02,880
met right here.

356
00:35:04,199 --> 00:35:07,039
Her fiancé painted a portrait of her

357
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:10,800
and made wine for her from the grapes here.

358
00:35:12,599 --> 00:35:13,760
It's a very romantic story.

359
00:35:14,719 --> 00:35:16,119
It's the very wine we're drinking today.

360
00:35:19,079 --> 00:35:20,360
The vintage of this wine is...

361
00:35:23,079 --> 00:35:23,960
three years.

362
00:35:25,079 --> 00:35:28,679
But her fiancé wasn't around to see it.

363
00:35:30,679 --> 00:35:31,960
He left before it was ready.

364
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:34,599
Three years.

365
00:35:36,679 --> 00:35:37,880
Freshly made wine

366
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:40,039
always carries a bitter taste,

367
00:35:40,519 --> 00:35:41,559
just like parting.

368
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,480
But in another two years,

369
00:35:44,039 --> 00:35:46,280
that bitterness will slowly fade away.

370
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:49,199
Time changes everything.

371
00:35:50,079 --> 00:35:50,880
I don't believe that.

372
00:35:52,559 --> 00:35:55,519
Many things never change.

373
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:57,599
People...

374
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,960
can't always live in the past.

375
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:04,880
I don't have a past.

376
00:36:06,760 --> 00:36:08,519
I've lost my entire past.

377
00:36:21,760 --> 00:36:22,679
I can't find

378
00:36:24,639 --> 00:36:26,280
the one I once loved the most.

379
00:36:29,639 --> 00:36:30,639
I can't remember.

380
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:35,440
That love once etched into my soul,

381
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:38,599
that I thought I'd never forget,

382
00:36:43,239 --> 00:36:47,039
has now turned into a melody,

383
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:49,559
a glass of red wine,

384
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:53,599
and some fragmented memories.

385
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:16,639
Actually,

386
00:37:17,480 --> 00:37:19,519
forgetting isn't necessarily a bad thing.

387
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:22,440
Obsessing over what's lost is just clinging to the past.

388
00:37:22,639 --> 00:37:23,800
No boat stands still,

389
00:37:24,719 --> 00:37:25,800
and no water stops flowing.

390
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,159
That's not fair.

391
00:37:27,159 --> 00:37:28,239
It is fair.

392
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:31,840
That kind of fairness takes a long time to prove.

393
00:37:33,880 --> 00:37:35,000
Don't be afraid of time,

394
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:38,400
and don't fear forgetting.

395
00:37:42,840 --> 00:37:44,079
Every day should be—

396
00:37:46,119 --> 00:37:47,880
should be cherished as dearly as birth.

397
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:48,599
Because

398
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:52,159
birth is just as fortunate as death.

399
00:38:21,519 --> 00:38:23,119
I really want to find

400
00:38:24,679 --> 00:38:26,480
the one I loved the most,

401
00:38:31,719 --> 00:38:33,159
keep loving each other,

402
00:38:37,880 --> 00:38:39,239
just like before,

403
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,880
and live a wonderful life.

404
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:45,119
Maybe...

405
00:38:47,519 --> 00:38:48,960
maybe he doesn't feel the same.

406
00:38:59,280 --> 00:39:00,400
Just got some sand in my eye.

407
00:39:35,199 --> 00:39:37,960
Well, enjoy your wine here, then.

408
00:39:38,039 --> 00:39:39,039
This wine is really good.

409
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:45,239
Captain.

410
00:39:51,039 --> 00:39:51,719
What is it?

411
00:39:51,719 --> 00:39:53,159
Here's the info I just found out.

412
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:54,800
He's an assassin working for Hades.

413
00:39:54,800 --> 00:39:55,639
Named Charon.

414
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:05,639
This wine really tastes great.

415
00:40:05,639 --> 00:40:06,360
Rosie.

416
00:40:09,519 --> 00:40:12,400
I haven't had the chance to talk to you about the wine,

417
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:13,760
or thank you yet.

418
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:15,119
So I'd like to propose a toast to you.

419
00:40:15,119 --> 00:40:17,639
Because without you, it could've been a disaster.

420
00:40:18,239 --> 00:40:19,280
Don't be so polite.

421
00:40:19,400 --> 00:40:21,320
I was more than happy to help her.

422
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,719
Actually, I really envy her.

423
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:28,239
And who is this?

424
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:33,360
I haven't asked his name yet.

425
00:40:35,519 --> 00:40:36,320
Excuse me...

426
00:40:41,159 --> 00:40:41,880
He's too dangerous.

427
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:43,559
We must get Anda and Rosie away from him.

428
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:49,119
Anda, listen.

429
00:40:49,119 --> 00:40:50,840
I found a wine you haven't tried before.

430
00:40:50,840 --> 00:40:51,599
Come on, over here.

431
00:41:03,519 --> 00:41:04,320
Let's go.

432
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:23,719
What are you doing?

433
00:41:25,280 --> 00:41:26,360
Fall back, fall back!

434
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:32,440
Why are you taking her away?

435
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:33,559
Who are you?

436
00:41:34,360 --> 00:41:35,920
What's your relationship with Rosie?

437
00:41:36,360 --> 00:41:37,239
Tell me!

438
00:41:38,079 --> 00:41:38,880
If you won't talk,

439
00:41:39,679 --> 00:41:41,719
I'll never let Rosie see you again.

440
00:41:44,599 --> 00:41:45,400
Wei Tian.

441
00:42:54,079 --> 00:42:55,800
Why did you betray Hades,

442
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:57,360
and even kill our comrades?

443
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:58,960
Hades...

444
00:42:59,159 --> 00:43:00,760
He gave us new life.

445
00:43:01,199 --> 00:43:03,360
We must fight to the end for his cause.

446
00:43:05,440 --> 00:43:08,480
You know what? Charon isn't my real name.

447
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:11,280
My name is Qin Huan.

448
00:43:12,480 --> 00:43:13,519
I'm Chinese.

449
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:16,679
I was a tourist kidnapped by the Hades Syndicate.

450
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:21,239
They captured me, controlled me,

451
00:43:21,960 --> 00:43:24,360
and trained me as a hitman to kill for them.

452
00:43:25,320 --> 00:43:27,559
Comrades? What a joke.

453
00:43:29,440 --> 00:43:32,239
Do you even know who you guys are?

454
00:43:33,360 --> 00:43:35,039
Do you know who you are?
